    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.test\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently `expect.reference_screenshot` places all screenshots in `tests/screenshots/` directory. Also it accepts a complete path to the screenshot. I think it can be useful to define the default directory to store screenshots. And allow to override it per `expect.reference_screenshot`. Why? Because the logic to generate the unique filenames is still useful, but I would like to store screenshots closer to the actual tests, not in a big pile in one directory. Potentially the option can also be a function that returns a screenshot directory for the current test file.",
